# Copy this file to `.env`. It holds only non-secret config (PROVIDER).
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Your API key is NOT stored here or in .env. See "API keys" below and
# ../SECRETS.md. (.env is in .gitignore regardless; never commit it.)

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pick your stack.
#
#   mock    -> a deterministic, offline, in-process model. No key, no network,
#              no cost. This is the default, and most of this repo runs on it.
#   openai  -> OpenAI chat completions   (needs OPENAI_API_KEY)
#   claude  -> Anthropic messages        (needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
#
# Twelve of the thirteen examples never need a real key: the lessons about
# promises, cancellation, discriminated unions, validation and the event loop
# are all visible offline. The one that genuinely needs a real model says so in the README.
#
# If you set openai or claude and the key is missing, the repo degrades to the
# mock LOUDLY (a banner on stderr, and every example's provider line says
# FALLBACK). Set PROVIDER_STRICT=1 to make a missing key a hard error instead,
# which is what you want in CI.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROVIDER=mock

# --- API keys are NOT stored here ---
# Your key never goes in this file or in .env. Store it in your OS keychain and
# inject it per-command with `secrun` (2-minute setup: ../SECRETS.md), then run
# key-using scripts as:  secrun npx tsx examples/...
#   PROVIDER=openai  needs  OPENAI_API_KEY     https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#   PROVIDER=claude  needs  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys

# Uncomment to turn a missing key into an error instead of a mock fallback.
# PROVIDER_STRICT=1
